            <ArticleTitle>[Treatment of angina pectoris by physical loading].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>467-77</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>21 chronic anginal patients (AP), 23 patients with an overall number of 37 aorta-to-coronary artery by-passes (ACB) underwent a regular physical training (cycle, quick or uphill walking, gymnastics). The patients were compared to themselves in the course of a calibrated effort test, performed until angina occured or the maximal cardiac rate reached.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
